# sasa.in — solvent-accessible surface area of the complex and of the ligand
#
# Ligand SASA is computed within the complex: the surrounding protein occludes
# part of the ligand surface, so lower values mean the ligand is more deeply
# buried in the pocket. This distinguishes repositioning inside the site from
# displacement out of it — something ligand RMSD alone cannot resolve.
#
# Usage: cpptraj -i sasa.in > sasa.log 2>&1
# Replace SYSTEM, REP, LIG and NRES before running.

parm SYSTEM_dry.prmtop

# Stride of 10 (one frame every 100 ps). surf is far slower than rmsd —
# roughly 6 min per trajectory at this sampling, ~1 h without the stride.
# SASA varies smoothly, so 500 frames are enough.
trajin SYSTEM_prod_REP_dry.nc 1 5000 10

# Whole complex: protein + ligand. Control for the overall fold.
surf complex :1-NRES out sasa_complex_REP.dat

# Ligand only, occluded by the protein around it.
surf ligand :LIG out sasa_ligand_REP.dat

go

# Notes from the log worth checking:
#   - probe radius is 1.4 A (reported as "van der Waals offset")
#   - LCPO is defined for heavy atoms only, so the atom count used in the
#     calculation is lower than the mask count (hydrogens are excluded)
#   - any warning about missing LCPO parameters means the ligand surface
#     would be underestimated
